    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4822c0e_2ac6727f",
        "filename": "runtime/arch/x86_64/native_entrypoints_x86_64.S",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T22:24:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes it does need to be called however this is only the native part of the generic JNI trampoline. It will be called after this function returns by the interception in the simulator as shown in the following code flow.\n\n1. `art_quick_generic_jni_trampoline` (Arm64) is called as normal and is simulated until `artArm64SimulatorGenericJNIPlaceholder` is called and intercepted by the simulator.\n2. `artArm64SimulatorGenericJNIPlaceholder` is intercepted and instead calls `art_quick_generic_jni_trampoline_simulator` (x86_64) **and** `artQuickGenericJniEndTrampoline` -- see https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680027/9/simulator/code_simulator_arm64.cc#120\n3. The result gets written to the correct registers and simulation is resumed in `art_quick_generic_jni_trampoline` (Arm64).",
      "parentUuid": "dd475add_cd2ffef6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 199,
        "endChar": 14
      },
